BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Curtain Up: En boca de artista 3 — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261029T203000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261029T203000
DTSTAMP:20261028T054808Z
UID:193451d160dc6199aa04cac76240@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:En boca de artista returns—a series that shines a spotlight 
 on creators and their creative processes. On this occasion\, the conversat
 ions will focus on the research currently being developed at the CRA by th
 e Art and Environment residents. This first session will explore botany\, 
 the language used to classify flowers\, and natural history\, intersecting
  these concepts with speculative fiction and archaeologies of the future. 
 The first session will take place on October 29 and will be divided into t
 wo parts: Part One: Ignacio García Sánchez and Ana Robles Pérez will be
 gin the session with a conversation alongside artist\, educator\, and rese
 archer Bárbara Fluxá . Immersed in contemporary speculati\nCategory: Mul
 tidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedu
 le/curtain-en-boca-de-artista-3
LOCATION:Nave 16. Centro de residencias\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 
 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/curtain-en-boca-de-artista-
 3
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossroads. El viaje circular de Boa Mistura — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261030T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261030T190000
DTSTAMP:20261028T054808Z
UID:c45a9ecd5cf31f52b6eab646ca5e@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:La periferia de Ciudad del Cabo\, Sudáfrica\, es el epicentro
  de un inspirador viaje a través del trabajo de Boa Mistura\, colectivo a
 rtístico de proyección internacional con raíces en el graffiti y el art
 e urbano. En el camino\, el arte urbano se convierte en el vehículo que c
 onecta las vidas de un vecino de una favela en São Paulo\, un joven del s
 lum de Kibera\, en Kenia\, una indígena mapuche en el norte de Chile\, un
  refugiado sirio y una mujer de una población pesquera de República Domi
 nicana. Estos pequeños encuentros a través de la pintura son la semilla 
 de cambios tanto en los vecinos de las comunidades como en el colectivo. >
  Encuentro posterior con los artistas de Boa Mistura.\nCategory: Multidisc
 iplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/fil
 m-series-madrid-landscape
LOCATION:Sala Azcona\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/film-series-madrid-landscap
 e
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ALERT: MINI-MONSTERS! — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261030T200000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261031T140000
DTSTAMP:20261028T054808Z
UID:214278bae5a9d5ff48247e10e551@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:Led by illustrator Emo Díaz\, this workshop invites us to tra
 nsform into our favorite monster by creating our own spooky masks using ca
 rdboard\, paper\, and everyday materials. It’s an exercise that encourag
 es imagination\, experimentation\, and giving shape to new ideas while wor
 king together as a family. Emo Díaz is an illustrator\, graphic designer
 \, and animator based in Madrid. He is renowned for his friendly\, colorfu
 l\, and approachable style\, which resonates strongly with children throug
 h soft-shaped characters and visual universes filled with joy and a subtle
  touch of nostalgia. As a children's book author and creative project crea
 tor\, he is also a regular workshop leader in cultural and edu\nCategory: 
 Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/sch
 edule/alert-mini-monsters
LOCATION:Taller\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/alert-mini-monsters
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Led Silhouette — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261030T200000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261031T220000
DTSTAMP:20261028T054808Z
UID:0991992152c91ed31a88b7a85b1d@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:A proposal born out of collapse—emotional\, climatic\, and p
 olitical—blending dance\, theatre\, and cinema. A work that explores hum
 an contradictions\, addressing themes such as isolation and social decay. 
 A reflection on our fragility in a world that seems to be falling apart\, 
 and an urgent call to look at the present. ULTIMATUM emerges from reflecti
 ng on how we coexist with the feeling that the world is moving towards ine
 vitable conflicts while we continue to act as though we bear no responsibi
 lity\, examining the boundaries we set\, what we defend as our own\, and w
 hat we are willing to lose or take away. This contemporary dance piece by 
 Led Silhouette (winners of El Ojo Crítico Dance Award 2024)\nCategory: Mu
 ltidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/sched
 ule/led-silhouette
LOCATION:Centro Danza Matadero\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/led-silhouette
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What Cannot Be Spoken About\, Better Ask a Ghost — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261031T170030
DTEND;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261031T170030
DTSTAMP:20261028T054808Z
UID:d80ddd507f49ce2d885e1e5e90cc@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:The Night of the Dead\, All Hallows' Eve\, Halloween Eve… On
  October 31\, we gather to conclude the project Culturas del duelo al sur 
 de Madrid ( Cultures of Grief in Southern Madrid ) by Inés Plasencia Camp
 s\, part of the Intermediae Distribuido programme. It will be a day dedica
 ted to discussing grief as a process that generates culture\, art\, memory
 \, languages\, and belonging along its way. A process shaped by material a
 nd political conditions that profoundly affect how we die and grieve\, but
  also by the possibilities that open up when thinking from its heterogenei
 ty and the forms of memory that have brought it to where it is today. Prog
 ramme Part One (5:00 PM – 7:00 PM) Layla Martínez \, Lloron\nCategory: 
 Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/sch
 edule/what-cannot-be-spoken-about-better-ask-ghost
LOCATION:Nave 17. Aulario\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/what-cannot-be-spoken-about
 -better-ask-ghost
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
